Modified by offline-speech, 2026-11-10.

Request IPA without a separator between phonemes in synth_ipa_ (emscripten/espeakng_glue.cpp).
With the space separator, this eSpeak NG version puts a space between every phoneme; kokoro-js
expects joined phonemes with spaces only between words, which is the output of phonemizer 1.2.1.

diff --git a/emscripten/espeakng_glue.cpp b/emscripten/espeakng_glue.cpp
index 24398dc1..6d2c3dce 100644
--- a/emscripten/espeakng_glue.cpp
+++ b/emscripten/espeakng_glue.cpp
@@ -62,7 +62,7 @@ public:
         
     int phoneme_options               = (1 << 1); // Use IPA
     int use_custom_phoneme_separator  = (0 << 7);
-    int phonemes_separator            = ' '; // Use a default value
+    int phonemes_separator            = 0; // No separator: phonemes joined, words separated by spaces
 
     int phoneme_conf                  = phoneme_options | (phonemes_separator << 8);
     
